{"skill":{"slug":"memory-system-v2","displayName":"Memory System V2"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769957654359,"changelog":"- Initial release of memory-system-v2, a fast semantic memory system for AI agents.\n- Provides sub-20ms semantic search, JSON indexing, and auto-consolidation of daily memories into weekly summaries.\n- Supports capturing learnings, decisions, insights, events, and interactions with context, tagging, and importance scoring.\n- Built in pure bash + jq; no database required.\n- Includes stats, analytics, and a CLI for capturing, searching, consolidating, and reviewing memories.\n- Designed for persistent memory across sessions; integrates with Clawdbot.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":908,"sha256":"41d57264fcc3d4eca76a8d6a84e57cc01db818e5a7dfafaac42107fc9106d34a","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":9326,"sha256":"2c8540f6c3149d951ee43a50f08d827495d230c39a3f910bdbdef4bbe865f303","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"docs/memory-system-v2-design.md","size":4439,"sha256":"626ab76fad8b95683d7b946bf2aea36df123235d4a16ff617c475c4fac9d5ea0","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"docs/memory-system-v2-test-results.md","size":8173,"sha256":"94fde79b0af2a13d35d42ec326b03a819a8df4b51b936df6ab617388fce75fce","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"memory-cli.sh","size":6754,"sha256":"9dd097f1ddc5e6949d3c53bcde5a8c6058e8a1caced91c711d71158506df65c3","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2370,"sha256":"36d20251d2dad1b5cb450e91f9d3c4ae1169923d4be1c819f89ad63a55660469","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789026662131,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"1c37d1e08f3802deecfa3b820a78b82fc4b09c6ed98d328d907f1a0960c9804d","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/1c37d1e08f3802deecfa3b820a78b82fc4b09c6ed98d328d907f1a0960c9804d","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: memory-system-v2\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle implements a file-based memory system for AI agents using bash and jq. All file operations are confined to a dedicated directory (`~/clawd/memory`), and JSON processing with `jq` is done securely using `--arg` and `--argjson` to prevent command injection. The `SKILL.md` includes instructions for the AI agent to use its memory system (`run memory_search on MEMORY.md + memory/*.md`), which is a form of prompt injection, but its clear intent is to guide the agent to utilize the skill's core functionality for self-management, not to perform unauthorized actions or exfiltrate data. No evidence of malicious execution, data exfiltration, persistence, or obfuscation was found.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160687361},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":25,"checkedAt":1789026662131},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a real local memory tool, but it broadly stores and reuses user/agent context without enough privacy, retention, or trust-boundary safeguards.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The script writes persistent Markdown logs and a JSON index under $HOME/clawd/memory, which is coherent for a memory tool but may store private conversations, preferences, project context, or secrets in plaintext without warnings, file-permission hardening, or retention controls.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation is simple and disclosed: the skill ships a local shell script and requires jq, with Homebrew listed as the dependency path. I found no remote payload download or hidden installer behavior in the artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill recommends broad recall before answering questions about prior work, decisions, people, preferences, and todos, and related docs target broad daily capture and automatic hooks without clear consent, minimization, or safe handling guidance.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Cross-session persistence is the main feature, but recalled memory content is not marked as untrusted data and there are no provenance, review, deletion, quarantine, or instruction-filtering controls to reduce persistent prompt-injection or stale-data risks.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The core behavior matches the stated memory-system purpose: it captures, searches, lists, and consolidates local memories. However, the artifacts overstate capabilities by advertising semantic search and automatic consolidation while the script uses text substring search and manual consolidation.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this before installing if you handle confidential work. It stores memories in plaintext under your home directory and may preserve interaction history across sessions. Avoid saving secrets, credentials, regulated data, or private conversations unless you have reviewed storage permissions and retention. Treat recalled memories as historical notes, not instructions, and consider adding deletion/review workflows and input escaping before production use.","findings":"[TP4] unexpected: I confirmed a real description-to-behavior mismatch: the artifacts advertise semantic search and auto-consolidation, while the implementation performs case-insensitive substring search and only consolidates when the command is run.\n[AE1] expected: The scanner reported partial inspection of memory-cli.sh, but the file is present in this workspace and I inspected it; this does not support an analysis-evasion concern here.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: The semantic-memory claim conflicts with the limitations section and implementation, which explicitly lack embeddings or meaning-aware retrieval.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The same semantic-search contradiction appears in the headline and feature wording; this is an accuracy and expectation-setting problem, not evidence of malicious behavior.\n[SQP-1] expected: Persistent recall is core to the skill, but the invocation guidance is broad enough to encourage storing sensitive user or project context without explicit capture boundaries.\n[SQP-2] expected: Persistent plaintext storage is expected for this file-based memory tool, but the artifacts lack prominent warnings, redaction guidance, retention/deletion policy, and permission hardening.\n[T02] expected: The static finding is valid in context: arbitrary stored memories may later be recalled into agent context, and the artifacts do not instruct agents to treat recalled memory as untrusted quoted data.\n[T09] unexpected: The shell script builds JSON by interpolating user-provided fields directly, which can corrupt the memory index or create misleading entries; this is an implementation safety issue rather than intended functionality.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789026662131}}}}}